Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:38:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] feat(workspace): constrain the imported bundle with a
 page CSP
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

QA3 I3: mountPrivateWorkspace() runs the server bundle through
`await import(blobUrl)`, so it executes in Formula's own origin and can
read sessionStorage.fs_auth_session and every fs_* key. index.html
declared no Content-Security-Policy at all, so nothing limited where
that code could send what it read.

Add a CSP that leaves reading alone (same-origin code always can) and
instead closes the exfiltration destinations: connect-src is limited to
'self' and the Supabase project host, img-src drops external beacons,
form-action and object-src are 'none', base-uri is 'none', and
script-src carries no unsafe-eval. 'unsafe-inline' has to stay while the
app has 126 inline onclick handlers.

connect-src and SCIENCE_WORKSPACE_API_ORIGIN are two separate settings,
so pwsApprovedOrigin() now refuses to mount when the configured origin
is absent from connect-src, with one console.error naming the cause. A
misconfigured deployment fails loudly instead of mounting a workspace
whose requests are silently blocked.

The residual gap is recorded rather than papered over: CSP has no usable
control over top-level navigation, so a hostile bundle could still leave
via location assignment. Closing that needs the bundle moved into a
cross-origin sandboxed iframe behind postMessage, which changes the
loader contract and both bundle modes. Not done here.

harness.js now inlines the suite instead of loading it with <script src>
— the harness page is opened over file://, where 'self' does not match a
sibling file and the suite was silently blocked. Both injected blocks
carry ids so the "no static Science content in index.html" test can
exclude harness scaffolding from what it inspects. harness.js also
asserts the shipped CSP is still meaningful before rewriting it for the
test origins, so the policy cannot be hollowed out while tests stay
green.

Tests: node harness.js 55/55 (5 new); LC_ALL=C ./tests/run-sql-tests.sh PASS.
Data structures: unchanged. Build stamp: 2026-09-05.4.
Critical Change — auth boundary; needs CODEOWNER @phossatron review.

